body:
Tested, everything in the preview works the same on my end, modified the testing project's main scene script to be:
```gdscript
extends Control

func _ready() -> void:
	%Button.grab_focus.call_deferred()
	%Button.pressed.connect(_on_button_pressed)

func _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:
	if event.is_action_pressed("ui_cancel"):
		%Button.press()
	if event.is_action_pressed(&"grab_focus"):
		%Button.grab_focus()

func _on_button_pressed() -> void:
	print("button pressed")

```
Pressing the ui_cancel button (escape) produces the sound of pressing `%Button` and "button pressed" is printed, exact same behavior as pressing the button.

> Still seems unused.

@akien-mga Regarding BaseButton's `focus_sound`, it's defined here so that it can be present in the class reference and editor theme item list. I do the same in FoldableContainer or LineEdit where the sound isn't used directly.

The sound is actually played here: https://github.com/Calinou/godot/blob/65e426f1bfc20e6df395300b285d017785666936/scene/main/viewport.cpp#L2438
